Node ID=31 the Saracen was yours
Text=Yours. <The voices come apart and knit again.> Then hear it as it happened: he was brave, he was the only one in that sanctum with a weapon that might work, and he asked the thing in his lamp for aid in front of a woman who had already agreed to accept it. We do not name him a traitor. We name him the man who did not read what he was signing, and we have had two hundred years to decide that this is worse. If his order has sent another of its sons, let this one read.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
